{"id":"000VXP","title":"Outervention (chaos construction, intervening cells)","author":"Chilly","solvedCount":0,"difficulty":4,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-14T14:14:34+00:00","posted":"Heute, 12:18 Uhr","rules":"This puzzle is part of the puzzle pack Chaotic Construction by the Sudoku Skunkworks. Please check it out!\n\nOutervention - by Chilly\n\nRules:\n\nChaos Construction: Divide the grid into regions of 9 orthogonally connected cells each, such that every cell is part of exactly one region. Place the digits 1 to 9 exactly once in each row, column and region.\n\nIntervening cells: An arrow in a cell indicates that a target cell, belonging to the same region, lies in the direction of the arrow directly after a segment of cells from different regions. That segment of intervening cells does not necessarily have to start directly after the arrow cell.\n\nOutervention count: The digit in an arrow cell indicates the number of edges that the shortest path within the same region from the arrow cell to the target cell crosses.\n\n6x6 example (not playable) showing target cells with dotted circles.\n\nSudokuPad - Penpa+","solutionCode":"Row 6 with a '-' for each region border, not including grid edges.","tags":["Sudoku","Chaos Construction (Variante)"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/0ukso5ws0n","kind":"sudokupad"},{"url":"https://tinyurl.com/29tndjzs","kind":"short"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/0ukso5ws0n","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-14T14:14:34+00:00"}